Package: yapacc
Architecture: any
Depends:
 ${misc:Depends},
 ${shlibs:Depends},
Suggests:
 yapacc-tui,
 yapacc-mcp,
 flatpak,
 curl,
 bubblewrap,
Description: optional companion to the native package manager
 yapacc (Yet Another PACkage Companion) works beside apt without replacing
 it. It tells where a package should come from, why something is installed
 and where it came from, and it gates and records the changes made through
 it.
 .
 It keeps no copy of what the native package manager knows, installs no
 daemon, timer, hook or alias, and its read commands change nothing.
 .
 This package contains the core command line.

Package: yapacc-tui
Architecture: any
Depends:
 yapacc (= ${binary:Version}),
 ${misc:Depends},
 ${shlibs:Depends},
Description: optional companion to the native package manager - interactive interface
 yapacc (Yet Another PACkage Companion) works beside apt without replacing
 it: source resolution, provenance, and gated, recorded changes.
 .
 This package contains the interactive terminal interface started by
 "yapacc i". Every action it offers is run by the core.

Package: yapacc-mcp
Architecture: any
Depends:
 yapacc (= ${binary:Version}),
 ${misc:Depends},
 ${shlibs:Depends},
Description: optional companion to the native package manager - MCP server
 yapacc (Yet Another PACkage Companion) works beside apt without replacing
 it: source resolution, provenance, and gated, recorded changes.
 .
 This package contains the Model Context Protocol server started by
 "yapacc mcp". An AI assistant connected through it can read and can
 propose; it cannot apply a change unless that is enabled in the
 configuration.
